---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { COSMOLOGY } from '../../../../courses/cosmology/syllabus';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
---
<CourseHome course={COSMOLOGY}>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>A new way to learn the universe</h2>
    <p>Most books give you pages of text and a few still pictures. Here, almost every idea moves:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Watch it happen.</strong> Ideas unfold step by step with Play, Back and Next, while the picture changes with the words.</li>
      <li><strong>Play with it.</strong> Simulations let you stretch space, heat a star, bend light or build a whole universe with sliders.</li>
      <li><strong>Physical meaning first.</strong> Every equation comes with a box that says what each symbol means in plain words and what happens if you double it.</li>
      <li><strong>Live problems.</strong> New numbers every visit, an instant check, a hint and a full worked solution.</li>
      <li><strong>Take it with you.</strong> Each lesson prints as a one-page summary sheet (save it as a PDF), and every figure downloads as a picture.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The course follows the real story: who asked each question, how they measured the answer, and where today's scientists still disagree. Real photographs come from NASA, ESA and other space agencies, credited under each one. Free, no sign-up, nothing you do is stored anywhere but your own browser.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
